---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/pages/privacy.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | LIT Bible"
  description="The LIT Bible privacy policy. Your reading life is your own — the site collects personal information only when you choose to send it, and the upcoming apps keep everything you create on your device."
  canonical="https://litbible.net/privacy"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "Privacy Policy — LIT Bible",
      "url": "https://litbible.net/privacy",
      "dateModified": "2026-07-10",
      "description": "The LIT Bible privacy policy. Your reading life is your own — the site collects personal information only when you choose to send it, and the upcoming apps keep everything you create on your device.",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@type": "WebSite",
        "name": "LIT Bible",
        "url": "https://litbible.net"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "LIT Bible",
        "url": "https://litbible.net"
      }
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="privacy-page" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">

    <header class="privacy-header">
      <div class="privacy-header__inner">
        <h1 id="privacy-title" class="privacy-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="privacy-effective">
          Effective date: <time datetime="2026-07-10">July 10, 2026</time>
        </p>
        <p class="privacy-lede">
          The LIT Bible is built on a simple principle: your reading life is
          your own. This policy describes what data the LIT Bible website
          (litbible.net) collects, and how the companion mobile apps are
          designed to handle data when they launch.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-body">

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-scope">
        <h2 id="privacy-scope">Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This policy applies to the LIT Bible website at litbible.net. The
          companion iOS and Android apps are in development and not yet
          released; the sections labeled "(app)" describe how the apps are
          designed to handle data and take effect when the apps launch. Where
          a detail is platform-specific (for example, iCloud sync on iOS),
          it is described as such — Android equivalents will be documented
          here at release.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-collect">
        <h2 id="privacy-collect">What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Website:</strong> The site collects personal information only
          when you actively submit it:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Mailing list:</strong> If you subscribe, your email address
            is stored by Brevo, which manages the mailing list solely to send
            LIT Bible updates. You can unsubscribe anytime using links in
            emails.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact form:</strong> Messages sent through the contact
            form (name, email, message) are delivered directly to our inbox
            by Cloudflare, the site's hosting provider — no separate
            form-processing service handles them. We use what you send only
            to respond to you; it is never sold or shared.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These forms are protected from spam by Cloudflare Turnstile, a
          privacy-preserving alternative to CAPTCHAs that does not track you
          across sites.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Cookies:</strong> The site sets one cookie of its own — a
          small flag (<code>lit_welcome_v2</code>) remembering that you have
          dismissed the one-time welcome message, so it doesn't reappear. It
          contains no personal data and expires after 30 days. Your reading
          preferences (such as the dyslexia-friendly font setting) are stored
          in your browser's local storage and never leave your device.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is privacy-preserving
          by design: "it does not use cookies, does not track individuals across
          sites or sessions, and does not build behavioral profiles." Aggregated
          data like page views and general geographic region cannot identify
          individuals. Cloudflare, the hosting provider, may log basic request
          data at the network level for security and performance, subject to{" "}
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>App:</strong> The app does not collect your name, email
          address, device identifiers, or identifying information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-reading-data">
        <h2 id="privacy-reading-data">Your reading data (app)</h2>
        <p>
          Everything you create in the app — highlights, notes, and your reading
          position — is stored in a private database on your device. The LIT
          Bible team cannot access this data.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you have iCloud enabled for LIT Bible, this data is also synced to
          your personal iCloud account via Apple's CloudKit. Sync happens
          automatically in the background, the same way Apple Notes and
          Reminders work. Your data is stored in your own private iCloud
          database; the LIT Bible team has no access to it there either.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can turn off iCloud sync for LIT Bible at any time in iOS
          Settings → [Your Name] → iCloud → Apps Using iCloud.
        </p>
        <p>
          App preferences like text size and display settings are stored in
          your device's standard preferences storage and are not synced to
          iCloud.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-content-updates">
        <h2 id="privacy-content-updates">Content updates (app)</h2>
        <p>
          The app periodically checks litbible.net servers for Bible translation
          text updates. During this check, your device downloads changed content
          with no information about you, your device, or reading activity
          transmitted to the servers. The process compares file versions and
          downloads updated text only.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-widget">
        <h2 id="privacy-widget">The home screen widget (app)</h2>
        <p>
          The LIT Bible widget displays lectionary readings and liturgical
          calendar information. All widget data is computed on your device from
          information bundled with the app. The widget makes no network
          requests.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-external-links">
        <h2 id="privacy-external-links">External links</h2>
        <p>
          The website and app include links to external services. Following
          these links subjects you to those third parties' privacy policies.
          The LIT Bible team does not track whether you visit these pages or
          take actions on them.
        </p>
        <p>External services linked include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Give Lively</strong> — for contributions to the LIT Bible and
            the Liberating Scripture Collective
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Apple Podcasts</strong> — for the Found in Translation
            podcast
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Spotify</strong> — for the Found in Translation podcast
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>YouTube</strong> — for the Found in Translation podcast
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>CreativeCommons.org</strong> — to display the full license
            text
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>liberatingscripture.org</strong> — the Liberating Scripture
            Collective's website
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-sharing">
        <h2 id="privacy-sharing">Sharing (app)</h2>
        <p>
          When you select text and choose Share, your device's standard share
          sheet opens. The selected passage text is passed to whatever app you
          choose to share it with. The LIT Bible team does not log what you
          share, where you share it, or frequency.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-third-party">
        <h2 id="privacy-third-party">Third-party software (app)</h2>
        <p>The app uses one third-party software library:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>GRDB</strong> — an open-source database library that stores
            scripture content locally on your device. It makes no network
            connections of its own.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          iCloud sync uses Apple's CloudKit framework, which is part of the iOS
          operating system and subject to Apple's privacy policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-children">
        <h2 id="privacy-children">Children</h2>
        <p>
          The LIT Bible website and app do not collect personal information from
          anyone, including children. The site and app contain no advertising
          and no social features. The only personal data collected — email
          addresses for the newsletter — requires active opt-in and is never
          required to access content.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-changes">
        <h2 id="privacy-changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If the policy updates in ways materially affecting data handling, the
          LIT Bible team will note it in the app's Translation Updates section
          and on the website, updating the effective date above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-contact">
        <h2 id="privacy-contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy can be directed to the LIT Bible team at
          <a href="/contact">litbible.net/contact</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
